[
  {
    "group": "How it is built and shipped",
    "items": [
      {
        "text": "One sbt build aggregates the <code>backend</code>, <code>ui</code> and <code>docker</code> projects.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "ref": "bootzooka:build.sbt:141",
            "quote": ".aggregate(backend, ui, docker)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The Docker image bundles the built UI as <code>webapp</code> resources of the backend (the UI is built with yarn and copied in as resources).",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "ref": "bootzooka:build.sbt:220",
            "quote": "yarnTask.toTask(\" build\"), copyWebapp"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The image is based on Eclipse Temurin 21.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "ref": "bootzooka:build.sbt:224",
            "quote": "dockerBaseImage := \"eclipse-temurin:21\""
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "CI generates the OpenAPI description, runs the tests, and builds the UI; the Docker image is published only from <code>master</code>.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "ref": "bootzooka:.github/workflows/bootzooka-ci.yml:44",
            "quote": "sbt \"backend/generateOpenAPIDescription\""
          },
          {
            "ref": "bootzooka:.github/workflows/bootzooka-ci.yml:48",
            "quote": "sbt testFull"
          },
          {
            "ref": "bootzooka:.github/workflows/bootzooka-ci.yml:58",
            "quote": "if: github.ref == 'refs/heads/master'"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "group": "Local development",
    "items": [
      {
        "text": "The UI dev server listens on port <b>8081</b>; the backend listens on port <b>8080</b> by default (<code>API_PORT</code> / <code>PORT</code> override it).",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "ref": "bootzooka:ui/vite.config.ts:16",
            "quote": "port: 8081"
          },
          {
            "ref": "bootzooka:backend/src/main/resources/application.conf:5",
            "quote": "port = 8080"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "In development the UI and the backend are different origins. The example UI env file sets the API base URL to <code>http://localhost:8080/api/v1</code>, and the backend installs Tapir's CORS interceptor with its default settings.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "ref": "bootzooka:ui/.env.example:1",
            "quote": "http://localhost:8080/api/v1"
          },
          {
            "ref": "bootzooka:backend/src/main/scala/com/softwaremill/bootzooka/http/HttpApi.scala:47",
            "quote": ".corsInterceptor(CORSInterceptor.default[Identity])"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Start scripts: <code>backend-start.sh</code> runs the backend under sbt with automatic restart and sets <code>OTEL_SDK_DISABLED=true</code>; <code>frontend-start.sh</code> runs <code>yarn start</code> in <code>ui/</code>.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "ref": "bootzooka:backend-start.sh:12",
            "quote": "sbt --server \"~backend/reStart\""
          },
          {
            "ref": "bootzooka:backend-start.sh:4",
            "quote": "export OTEL_SDK_DISABLED=true"
          },
          {
            "ref": "bootzooka:frontend-start.sh:4",
            "quote": "yarn start"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "<code>docker-compose.yml</code> runs PostgreSQL with its port published on host port <b>25432</b>, while the backend's default database port is 5432 (<code>SQL_PORT</code> overrides it).",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "ref": "bootzooka:docker-compose.yml:24",
            "quote": "- '25432:5432'"
          },
          {
            "ref": "bootzooka:backend/src/main/resources/application.conf:21",
            "quote": "port = 5432"
          },
          {
            "ref": "bootzooka:backend/src/main/resources/application.conf:22",
            "quote": "port = ${?SQL_PORT}"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The same compose file starts a <code>grafana/otel-lgtm</code> container, and the backend container is pointed at its OTLP endpoint with environment variables; Grafana is on host port 3000.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "ref": "bootzooka:docker-compose.yml:32",
            "quote": "image: 'grafana/otel-lgtm'"
          },
          {
            "ref": "bootzooka:docker-compose.yml:15",
            "quote": "OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT: 'http://observability:4318'"
          },
          {
            "ref": "bootzooka:docker-compose.yml:34",
            "quote": "- '3000:3000'"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "group": "Deployment to Kubernetes",
    "items": [
      {
        "text": "A Helm chart named <code>bootzooka</code> lives in <code>helm/bootzooka</code>; it can install a Bitnami PostgreSQL sub-chart (<code>postgresql.enabled</code>).",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "ref": "bootzooka:helm/bootzooka/Chart.yaml:4",
            "quote": "name: bootzooka"
          },
          {
            "ref": "bootzooka:helm/bootzooka/Chart.yaml:26",
            "quote": "condition: postgresql.enabled"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The chart passes settings to the container as environment variables from a ConfigMap and a Secret, including SMTP, database and OpenTelemetry settings; OpenTelemetry is off unless <code>bootzooka.otel.enabled</code> is true.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "ref": "bootzooka:helm/bootzooka/templates/deployment.yaml:26",
            "quote": "envFrom:"
          },
          {
            "ref": "bootzooka:helm/bootzooka/templates/configmap.yaml:19",
            "quote": "OTEL_SDK_DISABLED: \"{{ not .Values.bootzooka.otel.enabled }}\""
          },
          {
            "ref": "bootzooka:helm/bootzooka/templates/configmap.yaml:7",
            "quote": "SMTP_ENABLED"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The chart has its own workflow, <code>bootzooka-helm-ci.yaml</code>, triggered by changes under <code>helm/</code> or <code>.github/</code> (pushes to <code>master</code>). When chart-testing finds a changed chart, it lints it, installs it on kind clusters for three Kubernetes versions, and checks that the generated chart docs have no diff.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "ref": "bootzooka:.github/workflows/bootzooka-helm-ci.yaml:6",
            "quote": "- \"helm/**\""
          },
          {
            "ref": "bootzooka:.github/workflows/bootzooka-helm-ci.yaml:53",
            "quote": "ct lint --config .github/helm-ct.yml"
          },
          {
            "ref": "bootzooka:.github/workflows/bootzooka-helm-ci.yaml:103",
            "quote": "ct install --config .github/helm-ct.yml"
          },
          {
            "ref": "bootzooka:.github/workflows/bootzooka-helm-ci.yaml:124",
            "quote": "run: git diff --exit-code"
          },
          {
            "ref": "bootzooka:.github/workflows/bootzooka-helm-ci.yaml:9",
            "quote": "- master"
          },
          {
            "ref": "bootzooka:.github/workflows/bootzooka-helm-ci.yaml:43",
            "quote": "name: Run chart-testing (list-changed)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "In that workflow the job named <i>Publish Helm Chart</i> (push events only) consists of a repository checkout step and no later steps.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "ref": "bootzooka:.github/workflows/bootzooka-helm-ci.yaml:133",
            "quote": "name: Publish Helm Chart"
          },
          {
            "ref": "bootzooka:.github/workflows/bootzooka-helm-ci.yaml:138",
            "quote": "uses: actions/checkout@v2"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "group": "Conventions",
    "items": [
      {
        "text": "The UI's API client is generated from the backend's OpenAPI description, not written by hand.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "ref": "bootzooka:ui/src/api/apiComponents.ts:2",
            "quote": "Generated by @openapi-codegen"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "API endpoint errors are returned as JSON with an <code>error</code> field, and each failure type maps to an HTTP status.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "ref": "bootzooka:backend/src/main/scala/com/softwaremill/bootzooka/http/HttpApi.scala:45",
            "quote": "all errors are formatted as JSON"
          },
          {
            "ref": "bootzooka:backend/src/main/scala/com/softwaremill/bootzooka/http/Http.scala:61",
            "quote": "case class Error_OUT(error: String)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Passwords are hashed with Argon2id.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "ref": "bootzooka:backend/src/main/scala/com/softwaremill/bootzooka/user/UserModel.scala:70",
            "quote": "com.password4j.types.Argon2.ID"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Sensitive configuration values are wrapped so they print as <code>***</code> in logs.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "ref": "bootzooka:backend/src/main/scala/com/softwaremill/bootzooka/config/Sensitive.scala:7",
            "quote": "override def toString: String = \"***\""
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
]
